1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,610
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:05,060
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,400
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,710
I've worked in a warehouse

5
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:09,200
for twenty-eight years.

6
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:11,654
Ten-hour shifts on
concrete floors,

7
00:00:11,654 --> 00:00:13,890
squatting down and lifting
to load trailers,

8
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:15,380
walking miles up and down

9
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:16,910
that dock every shift.

10
00:00:17,353 --> 00:00:18,480
That's a lot of years

11
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,660
on a pair of knees.

12
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:20,680
I had my right knee

13
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,070
replaced two years ago.

14
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:24,210
It has hurt every day
since.

15
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,850
Not surgery pain.

16
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:27,700
I know what that felt
like,

17
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:28,810
and it went away.

18
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:29,940
This is different.

19
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:30,770
Tight.

20
00:00:30,961 --> 00:00:31,570
Full.

21
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:32,560
Like a band around

22
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,440
the joint that never
loosens.

23
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:35,410
And for two years I've

24
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:36,880
been told the same thing.

25
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,050
Give it time.

26
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:40,450
At six weeks it was
swelling,

27
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:41,830
and swelling is normal.

28
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:43,310
At three months,

29
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:44,400
give it six.

30
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:45,703
At six months,

31
00:00:45,703 --> 00:00:47,360
some knees take a full
year.

32
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,380
At a year,

33
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,290
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

34
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:51,720
And I didn't just wait.

35
00:00:51,829 --> 00:00:53,050
We went down the list.

36
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:54,600
More physical therapy.

37
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,030
Every session,

38
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:57,790
every exercise at home.

39
00:00:57,870 --> 00:00:59,120
I got stronger.

40
00:00:59,302 --> 00:01:01,130
The tightness never moved.

41
00:01:01,261 --> 00:01:02,760
The pain pills helped,

42
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:04,120
and that was the problem.

43
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,240
I'm already on enough
every morning,

44
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,290
and nobody could tell me

45
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:08,590
when I'd get to stop.

46
00:01:08,725 --> 00:01:09,910
Then a nerve block.

47
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:11,760
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

48
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,410
And after that, a second

49
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:14,550
operation to go back

50
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:15,580
in and do it over.

51
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:16,770
I said no.

52
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:18,550
Every morning I laced up
my work

53
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:19,680
boots and my knee felt
like

54
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,290
a band was wrapped around
it,

55
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:23,340
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

56
00:01:23,610 --> 00:01:25,220
Every morning I took
something

57
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,940
for it and clocked in.

58
00:01:27,210 --> 00:01:28,690
I couldn't squat down to
load

59
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:30,527
the bottom of a trailer
anymore,

60
00:01:30,527 --> 00:01:31,100
so they put me

61
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,320
on the pallet jack.

62
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:34,540
Couldn't stand on that
concrete long

63
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,640
enough to finish a shift

64
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,550
without shifting off the
knee,

65
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:39,420
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

66
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,680
without shifting every two
minutes.

67
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,430
It woke me at night,

68
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:45,580
and it turned ordinary
things,

69
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,835
like climbing up onto the
forklift

70
00:01:47,835 --> 00:01:49,410
or getting up off the
couch,

71
00:01:49,410 --> 00:01:50,530
into a decision.

72
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:52,810
After a long and serious

73
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:54,210
talk with my wife,

74
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:56,000
I went back in one more
time.

75
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:57,340
That was the fourth set

76
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:58,890
of X-rays on this knee.

77
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,650
And like the three before
it,

78
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:03,370
the answer was everything
looks great.

79
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,800
No loosening, no
infection,

80
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:06,860
nothing wrong.

81
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:08,100
Only this time

82
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,360
there was no new number.

83
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,710
Nobody said give it
another six months.

84
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,530
There was nothing left to
give it.

85
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,920
I sat in the parking

86
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:15,970
lot for a while.

87
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,730
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:17,790 --> 00:02:19,490
Then explain this.

89
00:02:19,730 --> 00:02:21,700
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

90
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,100
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:23,330 --> 00:02:24,190
I'd just come home

92
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:25,800
from a twelve-hour shift,

93
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,410
loading trailers on that
concrete

94
00:02:27,410 --> 00:02:28,770
for the holiday rush.

95
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:30,890
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

96
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,650
Everyone in the house was
asleep

97
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,190
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

98
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,339
with my leg up,

99
00:02:35,339 --> 00:02:36,730
trying to find any angle
where

100
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:38,290
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

101
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:39,660
around my knee and
tightening.

102
00:02:40,070 --> 00:02:42,220
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

103
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,930
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

104
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,490
And I just thought,

105
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:47,400
is this really my life
now?

106
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,570
Twenty-eight years on that
dock,

107
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:50,690
and I was starting to
wonder

108
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:51,850
if this knee was going to
make

109
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:53,750
me quit before I was
ready.

110
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,230
I can't live like this.

111
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:57,060
So I made myself a
promise.

112
00:02:57,170 --> 00:02:57,980
I wouldn't go a day

113
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:59,470
without looking for an
answer.

114
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:00,570
And when I found one,

115
00:03:00,570 --> 00:03:01,650
I'd share it with everyone

116
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:03,020
going through the same
thing.

117
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:04,530
So I got my laptop

118
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:05,710
out and went looking.

119
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:07,310
Not for a product.

120
00:03:07,643 --> 00:03:08,760
For an explanation.

121
00:03:09,050 --> 00:03:10,650
Mayo Clinic forums,

122
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:13,100
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

123
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,800
doctor videos,

124
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,200
medical animations.

125
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:17,770
And that's when I found a
video

126
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:19,590
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

127
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:21,800
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

128
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,630
had been through exactly
this.

129
00:03:23,848 --> 00:03:25,940
But before I say anything
else,

130
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,370
I want to be straight with
you.

131
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:29,870
You've already had
something work fast.

132
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:30,730
The ice.

133
00:03:31,017 --> 00:03:32,750
The first week of a new
pill.

134
00:03:33,052 --> 00:03:34,460
The good day after a
session.

135
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,940
Then it wore off.

136
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,510
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

137
00:03:38,925 --> 00:03:40,560
Fast relief isn't relief.

138
00:03:41,010 --> 00:03:42,030
It's a preview.

139
00:03:42,245 --> 00:03:43,200
So I'm not going to tell

140
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,500
you this works fast.

141
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:45,460
It doesn't.

142
00:03:45,739 --> 00:03:47,583
But if you're willing to
be patient,

143
00:03:47,583 --> 00:03:48,650
and to look at what's
going

144
00:03:48,650 --> 00:03:50,270
on around your new knee

145
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:51,650
instead of inside it,

146
00:03:51,650 --> 00:03:53,110
there is a real reason

147
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:54,300
it still hurts.

148
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,260
And something you can do
about it.

149
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:58,480
Let me explain what he
said,

150
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,610
because this is what
changed

151
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:00,710
everything for me.

152
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,600
He started with the
basics.

153
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:04,200
A knee replacement takes
out

154
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,800
the worn joint surfaces

155
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,800
and puts in metal and
plastic.

156
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,930
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

157
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:11,630
you had before the
operation.

158
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,350
That part I already knew.

159
00:04:13,934 --> 00:04:15,120
But then he explained
something

160
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,470
nobody had ever told me.

161
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:17,080
He said,

162
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:18,630
think about a swollen foot

163
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:19,960
inside a shoe.

164
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:21,590
The shoe didn't shrink.

165
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:23,953
Your foot is taking up
more room,

166
00:04:23,953 --> 00:04:25,630
so everything feels
cramped

167
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:27,340
and tight and squeezed.

168
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:28,870
Your new knee sits

169
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,320
in a limited space with
living

170
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:32,030
tissue packed all around
it.

171
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:34,070
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

172
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:35,680
had to work through that
tissue.

173
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:38,530
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

174
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,940
At first that's normal.

175
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:42,000
But in some people that
swelling can

176
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,610
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

177
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,510
And swollen tissue takes
up more

178
00:04:46,510 --> 00:04:48,210
room than calm tissue
does.

179
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:49,950
So when you bend,

180
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:51,620
that tissue gets
compressed.

181
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:52,910
When you straighten,

182
00:04:52,910 --> 00:04:54,180
it gets pulled tight.

183
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:55,570
That's the band.

184
00:04:55,716 --> 00:04:58,160
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

185
00:04:58,230 --> 00:04:59,240
And you start being

186
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,420
the one who says,

187
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:01,500
you guys go ahead.

188
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:02,580
I'll stay here.

189
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:04,550
And that's exactly why so
much

190
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:06,330
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

191
00:05:06,768 --> 00:05:08,700
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

192
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:09,570
around the knee.

193
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:10,640
Worth doing,

194
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:11,560
and I'd done it.

195
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,290
It does nothing about
tissue

196
00:05:13,290 --> 00:05:14,360
taking up room.

197
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:15,890
A nerve block quiets

198
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:17,510
the nerve carrying the
signal.

199
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,680
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

200
00:05:19,850 --> 00:05:21,410
But when that irritated
tissue

201
00:05:21,410 --> 00:05:23,180
finally calms down,

202
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:24,774
it holds less fluid,

203
00:05:24,774 --> 00:05:26,360
and it takes up less room.

204
00:05:26,610 --> 00:05:27,970
Less room taken up means

205
00:05:27,970 --> 00:05:29,920
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

206
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:31,800
That's what takes the
pressure off.

207
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,250
After two years of this,

208
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,740
it finally made sense.

209
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:36,500
The problem was never the
new knee.

210
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,350
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

211
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:39,820
He calls it the squeeze.

212
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:41,860
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

213
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,300
I'd bought knee sleeves,

214
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,840
compression braces,

215
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:47,100
gel insoles for the
concrete,

216
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:49,948
creams, half of Amazon
really,

217
00:05:49,948 --> 00:05:51,190
and all any of it gave

218
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:52,260
me was an hour.

219
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:53,590
I even looked at going

220
00:05:53,590 --> 00:05:55,460
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

221
00:05:55,590 --> 00:05:57,100
But at $200 a session

222
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:58,967
with nothing covered by
insurance,

223
00:05:58,967 --> 00:06:00,170
that was a quick no.

224
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,180
Then one night I went back

225
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:03,790
to that knee replacement
group

226
00:06:03,790 --> 00:06:05,010
and actually read it.

227
00:06:05,347 --> 00:06:06,680
Thousands of people,

228
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,314
years out from surgery,

229
00:06:08,314 --> 00:06:10,580
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

230
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:11,860
nobody could explain.

231
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:13,590
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

232
00:06:13,590 --> 00:06:15,000
the same thing kept coming
up.

233
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,790
This one device,

234
00:06:16,790 --> 00:06:18,450
and people saying it was
the first

235
00:06:18,450 --> 00:06:19,830
thing that made a
difference.

236
00:06:20,070 --> 00:06:23,039
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

237
00:06:23,039 --> 00:06:24,588
alright, here it comes,

238
00:06:24,588 --> 00:06:26,090
he's selling me something,

239
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:27,910
let me shut that down
right now.

240
00:06:28,070 --> 00:06:29,720
I'm only here because I
made myself

241
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,080
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

242
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,990
that if I ever found

243
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:34,050
something that helped,

244
00:06:34,050 --> 00:06:35,030
I'd say so.

245
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:36,750
It's called the KenRelief
Red

246
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:38,080
Light Therapy Wrap.

247
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:39,510
At first glance

248
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:40,530
I didn't buy it.

249
00:06:40,790 --> 00:06:42,700
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

250
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:44,860
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

251
00:06:45,208 --> 00:06:46,900
But I went to their
website anyway,

252
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:47,780
just to see what all

253
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:48,970
the fuss was about.

254
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:51,470
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

255
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:53,980
charge $200 a session for,

256
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:56,940
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

257
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:57,900
in a wrap you plug

258
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:59,040
into the wall at home.

259
00:06:59,370 --> 00:07:01,130
Two hundred and forty
lights.

260
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:04,140
Red at 660 nanometers

261
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:07,100
and near-infrared at 850,

262
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,370
run together for the
strongest effect.

263
00:07:09,539 --> 00:07:10,860
Four strength levels.

264
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,830
A five to thirty minute
timer.

265
00:07:13,019 --> 00:07:14,520
Then I saw the guarantee.

266
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:15,830
Ninety days.

267
00:07:16,050 --> 00:07:18,490
Results or your money
back,

268
00:07:18,490 --> 00:07:20,990
no questions, no store
credit,

269
00:07:20,990 --> 00:07:22,870
and you don't even send it
back.

270
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:25,670
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

271
00:07:25,670 --> 00:07:27,130
days to change my mind.

272
00:07:27,170 --> 00:07:28,380
There wasn't much to lose,

273
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,410
so I ordered it.

274
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:31,060
Two of them, actually.

275
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:33,400
Only the right knee was
replaced,

276
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:35,450
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

277
00:07:35,450 --> 00:07:37,360
and I'd done it for two
years.

278
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:38,750
Every time I squatted down

279
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:39,820
to lift a box,

280
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:41,690
I pushed back up off the
left.

281
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:43,810
The left one was carrying
the difference.

282
00:07:44,110 --> 00:07:45,200
When it came,

283
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,820
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

284
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,100
because I'd been let down
too

285
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:50,650
many times to get excited.

286
00:07:50,990 --> 00:07:52,380
What I felt was warmth.

287
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,170
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

288
00:07:54,290 --> 00:07:55,860
More like it was coming
from inside

289
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:57,840
the knee and spreading
around it.

290
00:07:58,190 --> 00:07:59,090
And that was it.

291
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,060
That was the whole
experience.

292
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:02,640
When I took it off,

293
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:03,840
I'll be honest,

294
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,580
nothing dramatic had
happened.

295
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,270
And after what that video
said,

296
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:09,530
that's exactly what I
expected.

297
00:08:09,750 --> 00:08:11,070
What was different

298
00:08:11,070 --> 00:08:12,080
was that for the first

299
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,610
time in two years

300
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:15,500
I'd done something for my
knee

301
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,550
instead of to it.

302
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:17,990
Twenty minutes,

303
00:08:17,990 --> 00:08:19,190
in my own chair.

304
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:20,700
No drive, no copay.

305
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:22,090
They say twenty minutes.

306
00:08:22,170 --> 00:08:23,010
I did thirty,

307
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:23,950
twice a day,

308
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:25,920
lowest setting that first
week.

309
00:08:26,030 --> 00:08:27,350
Once before my shift,

310
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:28,690
once when I got home.

311
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,260
I put it on the calendar.

312
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:31,580
The first week,

313
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:32,490
I couldn't have told

314
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:33,950
you if anything was
happening.

315
00:08:34,170 --> 00:08:35,070
I tried not to get

316
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:36,050
my hopes up.

317
00:08:36,090 --> 00:08:36,920
I'd had things help

318
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,340
for a week and then stop.

319
00:08:38,611 --> 00:08:39,870
But somewhere in the
second week

320
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:40,860
I noticed I'd come down

321
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,810
the stairs without holding
the rail.

322
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:44,360
I hadn't decided to.

323
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,601
I just did it,

324
00:08:45,601 --> 00:08:48,180
then stopped halfway down
because I realized.

325
00:08:48,450 --> 00:08:49,360
By the end of the fourth

326
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,430
week I'd slept through

327
00:08:50,430 --> 00:08:52,090
the night four times
running.

328
00:08:52,330 --> 00:08:53,270
I stood at the counter

329
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:54,680
and finished making dinner

330
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,200
without looking for the
stool.

331
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,820
None of that is dramatic.

332
00:08:57,860 --> 00:08:58,830
All of it was gone

333
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:00,090
for two years.

334
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:01,930
A few weeks later my wife
asked

335
00:09:01,930 --> 00:09:02,860
if I wanted to walk

336
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:04,640
the long way around the
block.

337
00:09:04,890 --> 00:09:05,870
And for the first time

338
00:09:05,870 --> 00:09:06,540
in two years,

339
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:07,650
I said yes.

340
00:09:07,750 --> 00:09:09,410
I wanted to understand
why,

341
00:09:09,410 --> 00:09:10,970
so I read the whole thing.

342
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:12,790
It comes down to four
steps.

343
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:13,530
One.

344
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:16,140
The tissue around a new
knee

345
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:18,320
can stay inflamed long
after

346
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,530
surgery is over.

347
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:20,170
Two.

348
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:23,040
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

349
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,080
so it takes up more

350
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,380
room than it should.

351
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:25,860
Three.

352
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,160
There's only so much room
in there.

353
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,630
Bending compresses it.

354
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,220
Straightening pulls it
tight.

355
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:32,620
That's the squeeze.

356
00:09:32,832 --> 00:09:33,390
Four.

357
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:35,220
Red and near-infrared
light have been

358
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,514
studied for calming that
inflammation,

359
00:09:37,514 --> 00:09:38,830
so the swelling and the
pressure

360
00:09:38,830 --> 00:09:40,020
can come down with it.

361
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:41,930
In a randomized trial,

362
00:09:41,930 --> 00:09:43,740
patients given light
therapy after

363
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:45,840
a knee replacement had
less pain,

364
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:48,680
less swelling and better
early movement

365
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:49,980
than those who weren't.

366
00:09:50,190 --> 00:09:53,170
A 2025 review said the
same,

367
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:54,460
and was clear the evidence

368
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:55,470
is still limited.

369
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:57,620
I probably sound like a
broken record

370
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,980
to the guys on my crew.

371
00:09:59,316 --> 00:10:01,080
But after two years of
doing everything

372
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,900
I was told and getting
nowhere,

373
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,510
you have no idea what it's
like

374
00:10:04,510 --> 00:10:05,950
to sleep through the
night,

375
00:10:05,950 --> 00:10:07,440
say yes to the walk,

376
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,080
and get my life back.

377
00:10:09,413 --> 00:10:10,460
So take it from me.

378
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,670
Don't spend another year
waiting

379
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:13,650
for it to settle.

380
00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:15,770
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

381
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:17,600
More than ten thousand
people

382
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,550
with pain after a knee
replacement

383
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:21,080
have already tried this.

384
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:22,970
Some had it worse than I
did.

385
00:10:23,230 --> 00:10:24,450
You can get the KenRelief

386
00:10:24,450 --> 00:10:25,930
wrap from their website,

387
00:10:25,930 --> 00:10:27,050
with a discount link

388
00:10:27,050 --> 00:10:28,820
and ninety days to try it.

389
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:31,020
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

390
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:32,270
you get your money back

391
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:33,530
and you keep the wrap.

392
00:10:33,632 --> 00:10:34,980
They only release so many

393
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,060
at that price.

394
00:10:36,310 --> 00:10:37,650
If it's still there,

395
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:38,490
get one,

396
00:10:38,490 --> 00:10:39,920
and stop the squeeze.

